\item \code{f}: The function to draw: a dm::Callback subclass overriding \code{call(double)}.
\item \code{from}: Left end of the range.
\item \code{to}: Right end; must be greater than \code{from}.
\item \code{n}: Number of sample points, at least 2 (default 101, as in R).
\item \code{label}: Legend text; empty (the default) shows no legend.
\item \code{color}: Line color (default red \verb{\{220, 38, 38\}}).
\item Returns: A new plot holding one Line series.
}
\item \verb{RPlot$qqnorm(data, label = "sample", color = <default>)} -> \code{RPlot}

Builds a normal Q-Q plot: the sorted \code{data} against standard-normal quantiles,
like R's \code{qqnorm(y)}.
\itemize{
\item \code{data}: The sample; at least two values. Consumed (sorted in place).
\item \code{label}: Legend text (default "sample", so the automatic legend shows one row; pass
"" to hide it).
\item \code{color}: Point color (default blue \verb{\{37, 99, 235\}}).
\item Returns: A new plot holding one Scatter series.
}
}
}

